      "writtenOn": "2022-08-05T10:40:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here is some pseudocode for the refactor I would suggest rather than this change:\n```cpp\nbool bta_dm_disconnect_and_unpair(const RawAddress\u0026 bd_addr, tBT_TRANSPORT transport) {\n  for (int i \u003d 0; i \u003c bta_dm_cb.device_list.count; i++) {\n      auto\u0026 peer_device \u003d bta_dm_cb.device_list.peer_device[i];\n      if (peer_device.peer_bdaddr \u003d\u003d bd_addr \u0026\u0026 \n            peer_device.transport \u003d\u003d transport) {\n        peer_device.conn_state \u003d BTA_DM_UNPAIRING;\n\n        /* Make sure device is not in acceptlist before we disconnect */\n        GATT_CancelConnect(0, bd_addr, false);\n\n        btm_remove_acl(bd_addr, peer_device.transport);\n        APPL_TRACE_DEBUG(\"%s: transport: %d\", __func__, peer_device.transport);\n        return true;\n      }\n    }\n    return false;\n}\n\nvoid bta_dm_remove_device(const RawAddress\u0026 bd_addr) {\n  auto currentlyRemovedAddress.\u003d RawAddress::kEmpty.\n  for (auto transport : {BT_TRANSPORT_BR_EDR, BT_TRANSPORT_LE}) {\n    auto connectedOnTransport \u003d \n      BTM_ReadConnectedTransportAddress(\u0026other_address, BT_TRANSPORT_BR_EDR);\n    if (!connectedOnTransport) {\n      continue;\n    }\n    auto startedDisconnect \u003d bta_dm_disconnect_and_unpair(\n      bd_addr, BT_TRANSPORT_BR_EDR\n    );\n    if (!startedDisconnect) {\n      // not currently connected, we can go ahead and unbond if this is a different addr\n      if (bd_addr !\u003d currentlyRemovedAddress) {\n        currentlyRemovedAddress \u003d bd_addr;\n        bta_dm_process_remove_device(bd_addr);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nI _think_ the logic is the same? And it should resolve the issue you hit in this bug.",
